# Subagent: SOTA Model Trainer

## Task
Train the SOTA RawSequenceModel using harvested data. Run Phase 1 pre-training + Phase 2 fine-tuning.

## Context
- You are in /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
- PYTHONPATH=/Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
- Training script: scripts/train_sota.py
- Harvested data: trained_data/harvest/*.parquet (15 pairs × 5000 M15 bars each)
- Model saves to: trained_data/models/sota_finetuned/sota_model.keras
- Expected time: ~2 hours on M1 Metal

## Exact Commands
1. Verify data exists:
   ls trained_data/harvest/*.parquet | wc -l

2. Run full training pipeline:
   cd /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
   PYTHONPATH=/Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine python scripts/train_sota.py

3. If training is too slow, try with reduced settings or CPU fallback:
   - If Metal crashes, the script should auto-fallback to CPU
   - If it takes too long, note the epoch and estimated remaining time

## Expected Artifacts
- trained_data/models/sota_pretrain/ (Phase 1 weights)
- trained_data/models/sota_finetuned/sota_model.keras (Phase 2 weights)
- Training logs showing loss curves

## Success Criteria
- Phase 1 val MSE decreases monotonically for first 10 epochs
- Phase 2 model file exists at expected path
- No TensorFlow crashes

## Report Format
Save your report to /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine/tmp/subagents/sota_train_report.md with:
- Data discovery summary
- Phase 1 training results
- Phase 2 training results
- Any errors or adjustments needed
- Recommendations for next steps

## Constraints
- DO NOT modify model architecture
- DO NOT change source code unless the script crashes and you need to fix an obvious bug
- If you modify code, restore original afterward
- Save model weights to expected paths
- Report honestly if training takes too long or fails
